# fleetboot autofs map: Kerberos-secured NFSv4 shared mounts.
#
# Mounted at /shared on every booted machine. Each subdirectory
# (e.g. /shared/teachers, /shared/students, /shared/all) maps to
# server:/export/shared/<name>. Whether the user can see what's inside
# is enforced by *POSIX permissions on the server* — sec=krb5p
# authenticates the user, then the group ownership inside the export
# decides what they can read or write.
#
# The placeholder <NFS_SERVER> is substituted at first boot by
# enroll-freeipa using IPA_NFS_SERVER from /etc/fleetboot/identity.conf.

*  -fstype=nfs4,sec=krb5p,rw,hard,proto=tcp  <NFS_SERVER>:/export/shared/&
